	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Installation de PostgreSQL 9 via Macports]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=8665#p8665"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Je viens de regarder un peu sur Internet.</p><p>J&#039;ai remarqué que ma façon de faire n&#039;était pas la meilleur, j&#039;ai réessayer : </p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>$ sudo su postgres
$ /opt/local/lib/postgresql90/bin/pg_ctl -D /opt/local/var/db/postgresql90/defaultdb/ start</code></pre></div><p>Et là j&#039;obtiens un autre message d&#039;erreur qui est plus encourageant :</p><div class="quotebox"><cite>Terminal a écrit&#160;:</cite><blockquote><div><p>server starting<br />FATAL:&#160; could not create shared memory segment: Invalid argument<br />DETAIL:&#160; Failed system call was shmget(key=5432001, size=29368320, 03600).<br />HINT:&#160; This error usually means that PostgreSQL&#039;s request for a shared memory segment exceeded your kernel&#039;s SHMMAX parameter.&#160; You can either reduce the request size or reconfigure the kernel with larger SHMMAX.&#160; To reduce the request size (currently 29368320 bytes), reduce PostgreSQL&#039;s shared_buffers parameter (currently 3072) and/or its max_connections parameter (currently 104).<br />&#160; &#160; If the request size is already small, it&#039;s possible that it is less than your kernel&#039;s SHMMIN parameter, in which case raising the request size or reconfiguring SHMMIN is called for.<br />&#160; &#160; The PostgreSQL documentation contains more information about shared memory configuration.</p></div></blockquote></div><p>J&#039;ai l&#039;impression que j&#039;ai toujours ce problème de mémoires partagées. J&#039;ai bien réalisé les instructions qui sont proposées sur la <a href="http://www.postgresql.org/docs/9.0/static/kernel-resources.html" rel="nofollow">documentation officielle</a>.</p>]]></content>
